            <ArticleTitle>Successful treatment of a saphenous vein graft pseudoaneurysm with PTFE-covered JoStents.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>569-71</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A pseudoaneurysm of a saphenous vein bypass graft to a first diagonal coronary artery is reported. The patient presented with worsening angina symptoms 14 years after her first bypass surgery when this diagonal graft was implanted. Angiography revealed a 3 x 3 cm pseudoaneurysm of the graft. The perforation site was successfully occluded by two overlapping polytetrafluoroethylene (PTFE)-covered JoStents.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
